                <pb facs="0739" n="1573" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/885</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-18T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 18, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.46 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3814. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 1895. Referring to telegram No. 595 from McFadden to you November
                        16.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d621-f1"/> The British have had in mind that the
                    present Dutch agreement is made with the Royal Netherlands Government and I
                    think they are disposed to tell the present Government that if a new Government
                    should be formed in Holland which was not approved by the Associated Governments
                    we would not be bound to grant the facilities according to the proposed draft
                    agreement. I should like to inquire whether you are willing to adopt this policy
                    and whether you are willing that a separate letter should be written to the
                    Dutch delegates saying that the agreement is signed subject to these
                    conditions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
